-- Walls further away are drawn darker, so distance can be seen as well as measured.
please define dimmed with a shade and a far:
    remember amount is 1 minus far divided by 15
    remember kept is amount kept between 0.18 and 1
    give back the rounded version of shade times kept
thank you for defining


please remember rows is the world
please remember ex is 2.5
please remember why is 1.5
please remember facing is 0.6
please remember playing is yes

please open a canvas 100 across and 64 down

-- One frame, written out as a real picture and put in a window of its own.

please repeat 1 times:
    -- Sky above the middle, floor below it.
    clear the canvas to the colour called "night" or 0
    repeat for every band from 0 to 31:
        remember up is 14 plus band
        fill a box from the point 0 and band to the point 99 and band in the colour with red up green (up plus 8) blue (up plus 22)
        remember down is 46 minus band
        fill a box from the point 0 and 63 minus band to the point 99 and 63 minus band in the colour with red down green (down minus 6) blue (down minus 14)
    thanks

    -- One ray for every column across.
    repeat for every column from 0 to 99:
        remember angle is facing minus 0.45 plus column times 0.009
        remember dx is the cosine of angle
        remember dy is the sine of angle

        remember far is 0.0
        remember found is no
        remember sideways is no
        keep going forever:
            remember wasx is the whole part of ex plus dx times far
            change far to far plus 0.05
            check if far is over 18:
                stop repeating
            thanks
            remember tx is ex plus dx times far
            remember ty is why plus dy times far
            check if a wall at with tx and ty and rows:
                change found to yes
                -- Whichever way the ray crossed into the square tells which face it struck,
                -- and lighting the two differently is what makes a corner look like a corner.
                remember nowx is the whole part of tx
                check if nowx is not wasx:
                    change sideways to yes
                thanks
                stop repeating
            thanks
        thanks

        check if found:
            -- Straightening the distance stops the walls bending outward at the edges.
            remember straight is far times the cosine of angle minus facing
            remember tall is the rounded version of 30 divided by straight or 30
            remember half is tall kept between 1 and 31

            remember bright is 245
            check if sideways:
                change bright to 165
            thanks
            remember wall is the colour with red (dimmed with bright and far) green (dimmed with bright minus 18 and far) blue (dimmed with bright minus 50 and far)
            draw a line from the point column and 32 minus half to the point column and 32 plus half in wall
        thanks
    thanks

thanks

